  writer while her sister amy studies  painting in paris and her oldest sibling  meg is busy marrying a schoolteacher  when the shy sister beth falls ill with  scarlet fever the family regroups at  their home in concord massachusetts  gerwig had been interested in this story  for a long time and had cited the book  as an inspiration for her becoming a  writer and director finding parallels in  her own creative journey and that of the  character joe  5.5  that's very generous  9  6 and that's it  mr dashwood if i'm going to sell my  heroine into marriage for money i might  as well get some of it  6.6  done  and you don't need to decide about the  copyright right now no i've decided  i want to own my own book  when sony first announced their plans to  adapt the book back in 2013 they had  attached screenwriter olivia milch but  after going through several producers an  alternate version was imagined and in  2016 gerwig was hired but not before  urging her agent to contact sony and  toss her hat into the ring of potential  writer directors gerwig's persistence  paid off and she was eventually given  the keys to the creative kingdom and  rightfully so little women was  commercially and critically victorious  it garnered six oscar nominations  including best picture best actress best  supporting actress best adapted  screenplay and best original score and a  win for best costume design just don't  get me started on gerwig not getting the  best director nomination  i cried 11 times in that movie 11.  the farewell lulu  is  young man  the farewell is a 2019 dramedy written  and directed by lulu wang it's the story  of a chinese-american writer named billy  wang who received word that her beloved  grandmother ninai has been diagnosed  with terminal lung cancer and only has a  few months to live bilia returns to  china under the guise of a fake wedding  to go bertley say goodbye to ninai why  covertly well because grandma ninai is  the only person in the family that  doesn't know she's dying the film stars  aquafina sema  dinan lin and xiao susan and was  distributed by a24 the company behind  the acclaimed films ex machina room  moonlight and the wildly popular tv  series euphoria  la la  wang's inspiration for the farewell came  from her own life experience which she  shared on an episode of this american  life in 2016.  in the episode wang discussed an  elaborate ruse that her extended family  orchestrated in order to bid farewell to  her dying grandmother much like the film  the family wanted the opportunity to say  goodbye to their matriarch without her  knowing about her own three-month life  expectancy i could see how some might  think that this is a pretty cruel tactic  but as wang's fictionalized mother in  the film poignantly explains the chinese  maxim is people don't die of cancer they  die of the fear so i guess the jury is  still out on whether this was a cruel  approach or not but one thing that's not  up for debate is that the farewell is a  heartfelt film with thematic depth and  well-placed humor and above all is a  testament to wang's brilliance as a  director  nomad land chloe zhao  the workhorse that is willing to work  itself to death and then be put out to  pasture and that's what happens to so  many of us if society was throwing us  away and sending us the workhorse out to  the pasture we work horses had to gather  together and take care of each other and  that's what this is all about next up is  nomad land a drama written and directed  by chloe zhao and released in 2020 set  in the south west we follow fern a  selfless widow who embarks on a journey  after losing everything during the  recession like a true nomad fern's van  becomes her home and her chariot  carrying her along the open roads of  america  the film is based on the 2017 novel  nomad lan surviving america in the 21st  century written by jessica bruder  hello coffee  i know you yeah hi dave right  yes  fern yes  have your uh can opener yeah yeah yeah  you do are you working here now or yeah  first year  so coffee shortly after the novel was  released actress francis mcdormand who  plays fern and peter spears decided to  option the film rights to the book  mcdormand had been impressed by zhao's  film the rider and approached zao about  taking on the project zhao agreed and  film began in the fall of 2018. similar  to xiao used real-life ranches in her  film the writer she also used real-life  nomads in nomad land giving both films  an unrivaled authenticity  nomadland took home three oscars best  picture best actress for mcdormand and  best director for zhao this made zhao  the first asian woman and only the  second woman ever to win best director  at the academy awards the first being  catherine bigelow  the power of the dog  jane campion  what is it george  oh you just  don't want to see how nice it is  not to be alone  and last up we have the power of the dog  a western drama written and directed by  jane campion based on thomas savage's  1967 novel of the same name it's the  story of phil burbank a handsome cowboy  whose true desires are hidden beneath  his rugged exterior phil's moods swing  from furious to cunning and he unleashes  his cruelty on his brother's new wife  and her sensitive son peter but as time  passes phil seems to take a liking to  peter and reveals a softer side when he  takes the boy under his wing teaching  him the cowboy ways i wonder  what little lady made these  actually i did sir  my mother was a florist  so i made them to look like the ones in  our garden  oh well do pardon me  it's somewhat open to interpretation  what phil's true intentions are with  peter but their relationship is  certainly tension-filled to avoid  spoilers i'm just going to stop right  there but keep one thing in mind don't  ever underestimate peter the power of  the dog features dynamite performances  from benedict cumberbatch kirsten dunst  jesse plemons and rising star cody smit  mcphee all of whom received oscar nods  for their work additionally the film has  been nominated for best picture and best  director garnering 12 total academy  award nominations the most of any other  film from that year so there you have it  our top selections for 21st century  movies directed by women as always we  couldn't include every title that fits  the bill there are far too many  noteworthy films by brilliant women to  squeeze into one segment but don't worry  there are plenty more episodes of rt  essentials coming at you so stay tuned  i'm sure we'll get there soon thanks  again for tuning in i'm maud garrett and  shout out to all the aspiring women in  film the future is yours  [Music]


